// [Claude, 2026-10-02] DENSE-VTK RESTART of the crashed job 4284723, from its own checkpoint at
// step 25001 (copied, not moved, from the vault archive's snapshots/ into
// build/apps/showcases/Antidunes/snapshots_restart_4284723/ -- loadSnapshot true here, pointed at
// that folder). 4284723 crashed at step 27344 ([STALE-PARTICLE-IDX], a downstream symptom); 80
// [MEM-GARBAGE-LINK] warnings preceded it, first at step 27338, with the first NaN normal at
// 27339. This run adds diagnoseNaNNormals + the full precursor-scan suite (denseNanScan,
// fluidSanity, low-rho/high-velocity/population precursors) windowed around 27200-27400, and
// switches the VTK snapshot schedule to a dense one: coarse every-100-steps coverage from the
// restart point through the approach, then EVERY step from 27334 through 27344 (the abort step
// itself), cropped to the hopper + full downstream channel (X 352-768, full Y/Z) instead of the
// original 128-640/Z<=100 crop, to see cylinder uid 2666130979403333644's run down the drained
// downstream sheet and the exact cell(s) where the fill~6e-12/density~7.7e10 MEM-GARBAGE-LINK
// event originates. timesteps cut to 27400 (24 steps past the original crash point) -- no need to
// run further. Same checkout/binary as 4284723 (no resync, no rebuild) per explicit instruction,
// so this restart uses the exact code that crashed.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// [Claude, 2026-10-02] CURVATURE-GUARD ACTIVATED: guardCurvatureInputs true added. Confirmed
// root cause and fix of the 192-rod doubling-series crash (job 4284164, step 9069, invalid
// quaternion) -- the rerun with this switch on (job 4284594) completed the full 51000 steps
// clean, 684 [CURVATURE-GUARD] hits, every single one the "non-finite neighbour normal" cause,
// all clustered at the Y=0 wall (Y=0.5-1.5), X~410-448 -- just downstream of the pillars. This
// run applies the same fix directly to the full ~406-rod production scenario, which crashed via
// the same general family of fluid-side corruption (reynoldsNumber NaN) twice already (jobs
// 4283504 step ~26700, 4283776 step ~26800, both with no other precursor warning firing) --
// per explicit request ("now run the full 400 rods with this fix activated and make sure it
// has the new vtk output timesteps as well"). VTK schedule (500/1000/2000/4000/8000/16000/
// 32000/49000) and 50000 timesteps were already in place from the prior skin-adapted run below
// -- unchanged here.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// [Claude, 2026-10-01] SKIN-ADAPTED PRODUCTION RUN: cylinderContactSkin 0.5 added (cd1b991b, rod-rod contact threshold a surface gap of 1 LU, rod-wall/pillar 0.5 LU), sealed-cell guard left off, matching the two clean doubling tests below this file's own production scale (jobs 4282267: 24 rods, full 51000 steps, exit 0, zero crash markers; 4282396: 48 rods, same result). The original/default --pitch=7.0 placed adjacent rows exactly 1.0 LU apart surface-to-surface -- precisely 2*skin -- which the pre-existing [RELEASE-OVERLAP] release-time guard mistook for an insertion-overlap bug (job 4282206, failed in 97s). Regenerated with --pitch 8.0 instead (real rod-rod gap now 1.52 LU, comfortably above 2*skin=1); every clearance (rod-rod, rod-Ywall, rod-floor, rod-pillar) is now asserted against its own skin threshold by this script (see the --skin argparse help and the asserts right after minsep/pillar_gap above). Rod geometry/count/densities are otherwise byte-for-byte identical to the un-skinned 406-rod original -- only the row pitch changed, same approach as the 24/48-rod tests (widen the gap, don't shrink the rods, per explicit instruction).
// hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidon_2node_skin0p5_gas.prm   (GENERATED by gen_hopper_clog_cyl_prm.py -- edit the script, not this file)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// [Claude, 2026-09-19] "HOPPER" CLOGGING SETUP, CYLINDER VERSION (THESIS_PLAN.md item 3/4). NOT RUN YET.
// Companion of the sphere hopper (prms/hopper_clog_pidon_2node_frontblock_gas.prm, same channel/pillars/PID/probes/VTK): two cylindrical pillars centred on the
// Y walls (X=384, radius 12, central gap 16 LU, plan view "|) (|") -- but the debris are CYLINDERS, diameter:length = 1:3 (r=3, L=18; the sphere's
// 6 LU cross-section), LONG AXIS ALONG Y (across the channel), released together from a block pressed against the pillars.
//
// KEY GEOMETRIC FACT: the rod length 18 is LONGER than the 16 LU gap. A rod lying along Y therefore cannot pass the gap broadside: it has to rotate its axis towards the flow.
// Expect jamming of rods across the opening (log-jam like) rather than the free arching of the sphere hopper -- a different mechanism (rotation-limited passage).
//
// POPULATION: 406 rods = 2 across Y x 7 layers x 29 rows in X (pitch X/Y/Z = 8/20/7.52, >= 1 LU surface clearance rod-rod / wall / floor,
// checked exactly for parallel cylinders). Only 2 rods of length 18 fit across the 40 LU channel, and each rod is ~4.5x the volume of a sphere, hence far fewer than the 1015
// spheres (kept: the same 29 rows, i.e. the same block length). densityRatio {0.5,1.0,1.2} = 116/174/116, stratified by height like the sphere version (1.2 low, 1.0
// mid, 0.5 in the top two layers; the top layer's axis sits at the waterline Z=49.13, half submerged).
// Block X in [141.0,371.0], front row 1.04 LU (surface to pillar surface, exact rectangle-disc distance) from the pillar cylinders.
// All rods are held FIXED for 2000 steps (settlingSteps, no startInactive) and then released together; clearance >= 1 LU so [RELEASE-OVERLAP] cannot fire at release.
//
// CONTACT MODEL: useAnalyticalContactDetection true (Cylinder x Cylinder = analytical Kodam+Guo HYBRID, usePureAnalyticalCylinder false keeps the GJK/EPA fallback;
// Cylinder x pillar/wall analytic regardless) + useContactFilterOwnerTiebreak true; every experimental contact/buoyancy fix explicitly OFF (see ModelParameters) EXCEPT useRotationalEffectiveMass (ON, user request 2026-09-20: generalised effective mass incl. rotational inertia in the contact law) and useTightLayer1 (ON, user request 2026-09-20: the capsule/segment-distance pre-filter for Cylinder x Cylinder; near-parallel false-positive fix is in PaperAnalyticalContacts.h + an always-on capsule bound).
// Friction/restitution as in the sphere hopper (0.5 / 0.5).
//
// FLOW/UNITS: identical to the sphere hopper (PID on, target 0.04, water Z=49.13, Z=180 headroom, <768,40,180> / <64,20,30> = 144 ranks / 2 nodes).
// CAVEATS: the upstream clog probes (X=336) sit inside the rod block (unusable as a clog signal, as in the sphere case); the fluid VTK is cropped to X 128..640, Z 0..100
// (the rods are unfiltered); the [CylComputation] contact-path diagnostics make logs very large (the 100-floater sediment run's log was 594 MB) -- expect a big .out file.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 64, 20, 30 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 0, 0 >;
   loadSnapshot                  true;
   storeSnapshot                 false;
   snapshotFrequency             5000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots_restart_4284723;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <768, 40, 180>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 2.0;
   floorHeightFactor  4.1393;
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
